BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195627@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260804T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T110000
SUMMARY:Hands on Impact: Friends of The Public Garden
LOCATION:Meet in The Lobby
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 4 spo
 ts left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/195627\n\nJoin fellow members and The 'Quin Impact Fund for a rewardi
 ng day of service dedicated to helping preserve and enhance Boston's belov
 ed public green spaces. Working alongside the Friends of the Public Garden
  - a nonprofit organization that has partnered with the City of Boston sin
 ce 1970 to care for the Public Garden\, Boston Common\, and Commonwealth A
 venue Mall - members will contribute to the ongoing stewardship of these i
 conic parks through a variety of hands-on projects.\n\nMembers will meet i
 n the Lobby before walking together to their dedicated green space. Volunt
 eer activities may include weeding\, litter removal\, fence cleaning\, and
  other seasonal projects dependent on park needs. This is a wonderful oppo
 rtunity to enjoy the outdoors\, connect with fellow members\, and make a m
 eaningful impact while helping preserve some of Boston’s most treasured 
 landscapes for generations to come.\n\n*This event is complimentary and re
 served for members only. We recommend wearing comfortable clothing appropr
 iate for outdoor work\, including closed-toe shoes\, and bringing a reusab
 le water bottle. All registered members will be asked to sign a waiver pri
 or to the volunteer day. Please click here to sign the waiver.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195627
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-196025@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260804T110000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T120000
SUMMARY:Art Tour: The Core Collection 
LOCATION:Meet in The Lobby
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Waitlist On
 ly\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/196025\n\nPlease jo
 in 'Quin collection curator\, Kate Chertavian\, for an art tour focused on
  the Core Collection. The discussion will begin in Bondo with Donald Lipsk
 i's spectacular statement chandelier and Christopher Wool's monumental sil
 kscreens and will continue with a thematic exploration of works on the gra
 nd staircase. With insight into the collaborative process of creating this
  incredible collection\, the tour will conclude in the lobby with artists 
 such as Julie Mehretu\, Auguste Rodin.\n\n*This event is complimentary and
  reserved for members\, plus one registered guest.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/196025
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
