BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-196895@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260804T170000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Taste of Puglia
LOCATION:Café Q
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nTime: 5 PM – 9 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/196895\n\nThis August\, Café Q invites members to experience A Taste
  of Puglia\, a limited-time menu celebrating the rich culinary heritage of
  one of Italy's most captivating regions.\n\nAvailable exclusively during 
 dinner service\, this thoughtfully curated menu celebrates the simple eleg
 ance of Southern Italian cuisine - think handmade pastas\, fresh seafood\,
  orchard-ripened vegetables\, creamy burrata\, and exceptional olive oils.
  Pair your meal with a crisp local white or a bold Primitivo\, and discove
 r the flavors that have made Puglia one of Italy's most celebrated culinar
 y destinations.\n\nMake a Reservation.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/196895
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195311@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260804T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T203000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Summer of Love" with Kerri Maher
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimited\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195311\n\nBookmark the 
 date for an inspiring conversation exploring “The Summer of Love” with
  author Kerri Maher. Moderated by Wendy Dodson\, owner of Humming Bird Boo
 ks.\n\nSettle into the sand this month and let the California coast carry 
 you away. A story of family\, love\, ambition\, and long-buried secrets\, 
 this is the perfect escape to pack in your beach bag this summer. Travel b
 ack to the Summer of Love in 1967\, where two sisters find themselves on v
 ery different paths. Winnie dreams of changing the world through poetry in
  the heart of San Francisco's counterculture\, while Miranda stays home to
  build her family's California vineyard into something extraordinary.\n\nF
 ifty years later\, Dawn Hartley is pulled back into her family's past when
  she sets out to uncover the identity of a mysterious bestselling author w
 ho seems to know all of the Hartleys' deepest secrets—including one Dawn
  is hiding herself.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for membe
 rs only. Light refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195311
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194363@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260805T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T210000
SUMMARY:Live Music: Anibal Cruz
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Available\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194363\n\nStep into The
  Reading Room for an unforgettable night of Latin jazz with Cuban pianist\
 , composer\, and bandleader Anibal Cruz. Known for his magnetic blend of C
 uban rhythms and jazz innovation\, Cruz has captivated audiences worldwide
 \, performing alongside icons like Paquito de Rivera and leading his own e
 nsembles\, Clave & Blues and The Blue Island Project. His set will take yo
 u on a journey through soulful compositions and dynamic improvisations. Ma
 ke it a night to remember with cocktails available from the neighboring Li
 ttle Bar or tableside bites from The Reading Room menu.\n\n*Please be awar
 e that seating is first come\, first served. Reservations are not required
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194363
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-196056@thequinhouse.com
